  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Sufentanil is a strong opioid used to treat pain, especially as an anesthetic adjunct and for postoperative pain relief. It remains in use, with an authorised product in the European Union, though it carries a boxed warning and is mainly used in controlled hospital settings such as anesthesia.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417915\">Wikidata Q417915</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>sufentanil</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>N01AH03</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00708\">DB00708</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/41693\">41693</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:9316\">9316</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417915\">Q417915</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C22H30N2O2S</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>386.554 g/mol (PubChem CID 41693)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>4 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
